//@version=6
// MNQ Noise-Area Momentum
// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// Intraday momentum from Zarattini, Aziz & Barbon (2024), "Beat the Market",
// with the paper's settings. Every half hour from 10:00 to 15:30 New York time:
//   * flat:  BUY if price closed above the noise area, SELL if below it
//   * in a trade: a stop order rests just past the noise line (0.24 noise units: the distance price
//     typically overshoots the line before resuming, from 16 years of data) and moves with the line
//     ("Resting stop", the default), plus a take-profit limit 1.5 noise units past the fill; or, with
//     "Half-hour check", EXIT when a check closes back inside the lines (REVERSE if through the other side)
// Everything is closed at the 16:00 close. No trades until 14 full sessions are on the chart,
// and none on the dates in "Don't trade on these dates" (holidays and half days by default).
// On scheduled Fed announcement days, no shorts before the 14:00 statement.
//
// Noise area for each half-hour mark = the day's open (and previous close) plus/minus the
// average distance price has moved from the 09:30 open by that time over the last 14 sessions.
//
// v3.8, 2026-10-31: for a 50K evaluation (docs/CANDIDATE_E50.md). 1 MNQ, at most $260 lost per trade (the whole
// position; the trade after a loser the same), so slippage keeps the realized loss under $300; take-profit 2 noise
// units; no limit on trades a day; max loss a day $900, so the day stays under the firm's $1,000 (as losses build up,
// each new trade's stop is cut to the room left instead of stopping); no extra contracts as profit builds; the
// evaluation tracker's target $3,000 and end-of-day trailing drawdown $2,000. In replayed 50K evaluations from every
// 5th session: 89% passed on NQ 2015-2025 and 94% on the index 2011-2026 (5-minute bars); in the Jan 2025 - Oct 2026
// window none failed and 84% passed, typically in 6-8 months, on 30-minute bars ($8,215, PF 1.78). Stopping for the
// day after a loss did not cut back-to-back losers (about 40% of losers either way) and passed fewer evaluations, so
// it is off. No rule prevents losing trades or losing streaks.
// v3.6, 2026-10-24: for a 100K account, with v3.4's rules (the best on the user's chart; v3.5's retuned settings
// made less there: +$9,467 against +$13,815). Max loss a day $2,000, end-of-day trailing drawdown $3,000 (stopping at
// the starting balance), a contract more per $1,500 of profit, up to 15; the evaluation tracker's target $6,000 and
// drawdown $3,000. For a 50K account: $1,000, $2,000, $2,500 and 8. Starting at 2-3 contracts went under the $3,000
// floor in early 2025 on the stand-in; from 1 contract no set ever touched it (docs/RESULTS.md, v3.6).
// v3.5, 2026-10-24: four settings retuned together: the lock at 0.45 max losses (42.2 points at $187.50 a contract),
// the range rule at 0.7, no shorts while yesterday's close is above its 40-session average (was 50), and no wider stop
// after a loser (the same $187.50). Chosen from 40 random combinations as the one better on the 2025-2026 stand-in
// and on both histories, and checked one step either way on each setting: the neighbours stayed close (stand-in
// 30-minute profit factor 1.88-2.08, no set under the floor), and 2 ticks of slippage cost about 13% (docs/RESULTS.md,
// v3.5).
// v3.4, 2026-10-24: back to a contract per $2,500 of profit (v3.2). On the user's chart v3.3 made the same as v3.2
// (+$13,778 against +$13,815) with a lower profit factor (1.43 against 1.61) (docs/RESULTS.md, v3.4).
// v3.3, 2026-10-24: a contract more per $1,500 of profit (was $2,500), still up to 8. With v3.1's trend rule the
// equity is smoother: steps of $1,500 never touched the floor nor stopped trading on any set; $1,000 got stuck on the
// histories; starting at 2-3 contracts hit the floor in early 2025. The user's chart ran v3.2 at +$13,815 (profit
// factor 1.61); on the stand-in this step adds about 37-39% (docs/RESULTS.md, v3.3).
// v3.2, 2026-10-24: the lock arms at 0.35 max losses (32.8 points at $187.50 a contract) instead of 0.25 (23.4).
// Retuned on v3.1's trades: on 5-minute bars better on every set (NQ futures 2015-2025 1.22x net, 1.42x net per
// drawdown; the Nasdaq-100 index 2011-2026 1.19x, 1.23x, 13 of 16 years better; the 2025-2026 stand-in's profit factor
// 1.65 to 1.91); on 30-minute bars about even (docs/RESULTS.md, v3.2).
// v3.1, 2026-10-24: from the user's TradingView run of v3.0 (1/2025-10/2026, 30 minutes): its shorts lost $2,179 and
// its longs made $2,117 in 2025, and near the trailing floor not one contract fitted, so it stopped trading for most of
// 2026. Now no shorts while yesterday's close is above its 50-session average (setting "No shorts while..."), and
// when not one contract fits, 1 MNQ with its max loss cut to the room left (setting "Never stuck"). On the 2025
// stand-in (NQ futures to July): v3.0 52.1% winners, profit factor 1.12; with the trend rule 59.0%, 1.47, the shorts
// +$976 instead of -$1,041 (docs/RESULTS.md, v3.1).
// v3.0, 2026-10-24: a $2,000 end-of-day trailing drawdown (settings "Trailing drawdown"), as at a prop firm: the floor
// is the highest end-of-day balance minus $2,000 and stops at the starting balance. The account starts at 1 MNQ and adds
// a contract for each $2,500 of profit since the start date (up to 8); no trade risks more than the room above the
// floor or what is left of the day's $1,000, a contract's risk counted from its own stop. At 4 MNQ from the start
// (v2.9) the 2025-2026 stand-in went below that floor 29 times; with v3.0 never, nor on NQ futures 2015-2025 or the
// Nasdaq-100 index 2011-2026. Stand-in 1/2025-10/2026, 30-minute: +$24.6k (v2.9 +$29.4k), profit factor 1.87 (1.48),
// 53.9% winners, worst day -$929, the largest end-of-day fall from a high $2.7k (after the floor had stopped at the
// start); 5-minute: +$18.6k (+$26.6k), 1.57 (1.46), 67.1%. NQ futures +$244k against v2.9's +$196k (docs/RESULTS.md,
// v3.0).
// v2.9, 2026-10-24: entries only near the day's extreme (setting "Entries near the day's extreme"): a long needs the
// check's close in the top 35% of the day's range so far, a short in the bottom 35%. A breakout after the day had run
// further and come back to the line made about nothing (profit factor 1.0-1.1 on NQ futures 2015-2025, the index
// 2011-2026 and the 2025-2026 stand-in, against 1.5 for the rest). Stand-in 1/2025-10/2026, 30-minute: +$29.4k against
// v2.8's +$27.1k, drawdown $5.9k against $6.5k, profit factor 1.48 against 1.42; 5-minute: +$26.6k against +$28.7k,
// drawdown $5.6k against $5.7k, 1.46 against 1.45. Histories: net 1.00-1.06x, net per drawdown 0.98-1.21x, the index
// better in 12 of 16 years on 30-minute bars (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.9).
// v2.8, 2026-10-24: fewer contracts, a wider stop, an early lock: 4 MNQ, max loss $750 (93.75 points; the line stop
// is usually closer), the lock at 0.25 max losses (23.4 points, then the stop to the entry + 2.5), the trade after a
// loser the same 4 MNQ with $1,000. Under the $1,000 daily limit 10 MNQ with a 37.5-point stop was stopped by ordinary
// noise and used up the day's room in one or two losers; 4 MNQ gives the trade room and the lock turns more of them
// into small winners. Stand-in 1/2025-10/2026, 30-minute: +$27.1k (v2.7 +$28.4k), drawdown $6.5k ($9.7k), 54.4% winners
// (42.4%), profit factor 1.42 (1.28), worst day -$918; 5-minute: +$28.7k (+$40.1k), drawdown $5.7k ($10.6k), 67.0%
// (49.1%), 1.45 (1.38). Net per drawdown on NQ futures 2015-2025 1.21-1.26x v2.7's, on the index 2011-2026 0.88-0.98x;
// net 0.53-0.61x on both. On the user's MNQ bars 8/24-10/16 (5-minute) +$2.7k against +$12.0k. After a full loser the
// $1,000 after-loss trade no longer fits the day's room, so entries wait for the next day. To go back to v2.7: 10
// contracts, after a loser 9 and $1,500, lock 1.0 (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.8).
// v2.7, 2026-10-22: at most $1,000 lost a day (setting "Max loss a day"), without a stop-trading rule. Each new trade
// may risk only what is left of the day's $1,000 (today's closed P/L counted, so a winner adds room): it takes fewer
// contracts with the same stop distance, and only when not even 1 MNQ fits do new entries wait for tomorrow. The
// losing-trade count limit is off (0): the money limit decides. Worst day, 5-minute stand-in 1/2025-10/2026: -$997
// (v2.6: -$2,8xx); the user's MNQ bars 8/24-10/16: -$921. The cap costs profit, because the strategy's good days often
// start with a loser or two: stand-in 30-minute +$28.4k, drawdown $9.7k (v2.6 +$83.6k, $16.4k); 5-minute +$40.1k,
// $10.6k (v2.6 +$95.6k, $11.6k). A stop is a resting order: a gap or fast market through it can lose more than
// planned (NQ 2015-2025's worst day with the cap: -$1,081) (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.7).
// v2.6, 2026-10-22: the middle risk. Max loss $750 (37.5 points at 10 MNQ), the trade after a loser 9 MNQ and $1,500,
// the lock at 1.0 max losses (37.5 points), 4 losers a day; the calm-stretch rule stays. The user's 30-minute chart
// 1/2025-10/2026 showed v2.5 ($1,500) below v2.3 ($500); the long histories, now without half days and data holes
// (positions carried overnight), favour a wider stop on 30-minute bars too, and the middle risk did best on the
// 30-minute stand-in and both 30-minute histories. Against v2.3, 30-minute: stand-in +$83.6k (drawdown $16.4k) against
// +$72.0k ($18.7k); NQ futures 2015-2025 +$624k against +$387k, the index 2011-2026 +$823k against +$645k, both halves
// better, no losing year. 5-minute: stand-in +$95.6k ($11.6k) against +$63.0k ($24.9k); NQ +$621k against +$375k, index
// +$918k against +$701k. Over 7/2026-10/2026 (the user's own MNQ bars) every version made about the same. A loser now
// costs up to about $750 ($1,500 after a loser) (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.6).
// v2.5, 2026-10-22: no trades after a calm stretch (settings "Calm stretch"): when the last 10 sessions' average
// 09:30-16:00 range is under 0.7 x the last 40's, no new entries that day. After such stretches breakouts of the noise
// area mostly failed. At every pair of lengths tried (5-20 against 40-100 sessions, 0.7 and 0.8) the profit factor rose
// on NQ futures 2015-2025, the Nasdaq-100 index 2011-2026 and the 2025-2026 stand-in, on 5- and 30-minute bars; 10
// against 40 at 0.7 is the one that kept the histories' net level (NQ 1.01x, the index 1.03x). Stand-in 1/2025-10/2026,
// 5-minute: +$112,731 against v2.4's +$109,026, drawdown $14,811 both, 60.1% winners, profit factor 1.64 against 1.58;
// 30-minute: +$71,111 against +$67,212, drawdown $17,524 against $18,354, profit factor 1.39 against 1.34. Also: the
// 2025 holidays, half days and Fed days in the date lists, for backtests from January 2025 (a position must not be
// held over a half day's early close) (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.5).
// v2.4, 2026-10-22: room for the trade. Max loss $1,500 (a 75-point stop at 10 MNQ; the line stop, 0.24 noise units
// past the noise line, is usually closer and takes over), the lock at 0.5 max losses (37.5 points, then the stop to the
// entry + 2.5), the trade after a loser 9 MNQ and $2,100, and no new entries after 3 losers in a day. The $500 stop (25
// points) was inside ordinary 5-minute noise: it cut trades that went on to work. Over 1/2025-10/2026 on 5-minute bars
// (NQ futures to 7/2025, the Nasdaq-100 index to 6/2026, the user's MNQ after; a stand-in for MNQ1!, not TradingView's
// own bars): +$106,385 against +$60,345, drawdown $14,811 against $27,577, 59.5% winners against 52.5%, profit factor
// 1.55 against 1.36. NQ futures 2015-2025: +59% net, profit factor 1.38 against 1.29, 10 of 11 years better; the
// Nasdaq-100 index 2011-2026: +35% net, 1.41 against 1.38, 12 of 16 years better. Every max loss from $1,000 to $1,500
// beat $500 on all three; above $1,500 the index got worse. On the user's 8/24-10/16 window it makes less (+$17,730
// against +$25,295, drawdown $4,129 against $2,613): v2.3 was tuned on that window. A loser now costs up to about
// $1,500 ($2,100 after a loser), so a day can lose about $4,600: too much for a $2,000 trailing-drawdown evaluation
// (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.4).
// v2.3, 2026-10-22: after a big day, no trades in its direction the next day (settings "After a big day"). After a session
// whose 09:30-16:00 range was over 1.5 x the average of the last 10, the next session's trades in that session's
// direction lost on average on NQ futures 2015-2025 and the Nasdaq-100 index 2011-2026. Without them: NQ futures +14% net
// and +39% net per drawdown (better in both halves, 8 of 11 years), the index +10% and +15% (12 of 16 years). On the
// user's chart window it skips one day, 9/22 (+$1,130 there): +$25,295 against +$26,425 (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.3).
// v2.2, 2026-10-22: no new entries from the 15:30 check (setting "Last check for new entries"). At v2.1's settings the
// 15:30 entries lost on average on NQ futures 2015-2025, the Nasdaq-100 index 2011-2026 and the user's chart window;
// without them the window makes +$26,425 against +$25,052 (drawdown $2,613 against $2,580), NQ +4% net, the index +3%
// net with an 8% smaller drawdown (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.2).
// v2.1, 2026-10-22: fewer losers back to back. The trade after a losing trade uses 9 MNQ and a $700 max loss (a
// 38.9-point stop) instead of 10 and $500 (25 points); a winner resets it. On the user's chart window (MNQ1! 5-minute,
// trades from 8/24/2026 to the data's end on 10/16): +$25,052 against v2.0's +$22,762, drawdown $2,580 against $2,934,
// losers followed by another loser 36% against 42%, longest losing streak 3 against 4. NQ futures 2015-2025: back-to-back
// losers 51% against 57%, net level, drawdown +16%; Nasdaq-100 index 2011-2026: 50% against 55%, net +10%, drawdown -15%
// (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.1; research/v22_after_loss.py). That trade risks up to $700.
// v2.0, 2026-10-22: fewer and smaller losses, more winners. Max loss $500 (a 25-point stop at 10 MNQ), take-profit 2.0
// noise units, lock at 0.75 max losses (18.75 points). On the user's TradingView window (MNQ1! 5-minute, trades from
// 8/24/2026; the bars match the user's chart to the dollar through 10/16): +$22,762 against v1.8's +$17,973, drawdown
// $2,934 against $3,100, 24 losing trades against 42 for -$11,392 of losses against -$14,026, 61% winners. On NQ futures
// 2015-2025 +30% net and +20% net per drawdown; on the Nasdaq-100 index 2011-2026 +12% and +12% (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.0).
// Four losers in a day (the daily limit) is about $2,070: above a $2,000 trailing drawdown, so on an evaluation set
// "Max losing trades a day" to 3.
// v1.9, 2026-10-22: more profit, fewer losers and a smaller drawdown. The max loss is $450 (a 22.5-point stop at 10
// MNQ) instead of $350 (17.5): the tight stop was hit by ordinary 5-minute noise. On the user's MNQ bars 7/27-10/16/2026
// (5-minute chart): +$29,506 against +$23,483, drawdown $4,161 against $4,181, 50% winners against 43%. On NQ futures
// 2015-2025: +14% net, -4% drawdown; on the Nasdaq-100 index 2011-2026: +1% net, 0% drawdown. Every max loss from $425
// to $475 did about as well; $450 is the middle of that range, not its best point (docs/RESULTS.md, v1.9;
// research/v18_scan.py). A single loser is now up to $450 + costs: four in a day (the daily limit) is about $1,850.
// v1.8, 2026-10-22: the stop only ever tightens (setting "Stop only ever tightens", on), as the NinjaTrader strategy
// since round one hundred and thirty-nine (more net in all four test periods, slightly smaller drawdowns). On the user's
// MNQ bars 6/29-10/16/2026 (5-minute chart, 10 MNQ, $350): +$24,296 against v1.7's +$24,078, the same trades and
// drawdown.
// v1.7, 2026-10-22: more winning trades, the v1.5 size. The lock arms at 0.85 max losses (14.9 points at 10 MNQ and
// $350) instead of 1.0 (17.5): on NQ futures 2015-2025 (1-minute bars) 51.1% winners against 48.8% for $132 against
// $129 a day at 10 MNQ; on the user's MNQ bars 6/29-10/16/2026 (5-minute chart) 49 winners in 112 trades (43.8%) against
// 45 in 111 (40.5%), +$24,078 against +$21,487 at the script's costs, about 6% less than 1.0 at $0.95 / 2 ticks
// (docs/RESULTS.md, "The lock dial, finely"; research/v15_lock_mnq.py). The evaluation trades 10 MNQ, as v1.5 did.
// v1.6, 2026-10-17: Account switch: Evaluation (3 MNQ) or Funded (10 MNQ), same $350 max loss and rules.
// v1.5, 2026-10-17: an evaluation tracker (bottom left): profit, trailing floor, consistency, what it takes to pass.
// v1.4, 2026-10-17: heads-up alerts five minutes before a check when a signal is likely (about 9 in 10 follow), so a
// trader placing orders by hand has the bracket ready at the check. Alerts only; no trade changes.
// v1.3, 2026-10-16: no new entries after 4 losing trades in a day (round thirty-eight: more per day, smaller worst
// stretch, on every period of both datasets).
// v1.2, 2026-10-16: the lock. Once a trade is as far up as the max loss per contract, the stop moves to the entry
// + 2.5 points (Tradovate's Auto Breakeven, 70 ticks / +10 ticks at 10 MNQ and $350). At that setting, on 1-minute
// data, winners went from about 14% to 48% of trades for the same money (docs/RESULTS.md, round thirty-seven).
// v1.1, 2026-10-16: optional webhook orders (TradersPost), for prop firms that allow automation (Take Profit Trader
// does not). Each minute of entry delay cost about 15-25% of the profit on 1-minute data (docs/RESULTS.md, round 35).
// v1.0, 2026-10-16. Tested on two independent datasets (docs/RESULTS.md): Nasdaq-100 index 1-minute data
// 2011-2026 and NQ futures 1-minute data 2015-2025. Per contract with $117 of room (the $350 max loss on 3 MNQ):
// about $28 a day on the futures data, t = 5.7, 10 of 11 years positive, about a third of trades winners; it
// survives double slippage, double fees and every setting nudged both ways (docs/RESULTS.md, stress tests).
// Most trades lose small and a few trend days pay for them. Not "never lose".
//
// Chart: MNQ1! (or the front-month MNQ contract), 5 minutes. 1, 10, 15 and 30 also run, but the take-profit and the
// max loss after the fill bar are checked once per bar, so a 30-minute chart sees them later than a trader would.
// The rules are the same as the Python reference in mnqbot/noise.py.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------
strategy("MNQ Noise-Area Momentum v3.8", shorttitle = "Noise-Mom", overlay = true,
     initial_capital = 50000, currency = currency.USD,
     default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1, pyramiding = 0,
     commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value = 0.62,
     slippage = 1, margin_long = 0, margin_short = 0, max_bars_back = 500, max_labels_count = 500,
     backtest_fill_limits_assumption = 1)

const string TZ = "America/New_York"
const int N_CHECKS = 12   // 10:00, 10:30, ..., 15:30
const int FIRST_CHECK = 600
const int LAST_CHECK = 930
const int RTH_OPEN = 570
const int RTH_CLOSE = 960
const int FED_CUTOFF = 840   // 14:00, the Fed statement

// ── Inputs
grpT = "Trading"
lookback = input.int(14, "Sessions in the noise average", minval = 2, maxval = 60, group = grpT)
funded   = input.bool(false, "FUNDED ACCOUNT (tick for the funded contracts; untick for the evaluation's)", group = grpT,
     tooltip = "Unticked: the evaluation's contracts below (1 to start since v3.0; more as profit builds, see \"Add a contract per $ of profit\"). Ticked: the funded account's (1). Same rules and the same max loss per trade; the stop and the lock scale with the contracts. At 10 MNQ and $350 (a $35 stop a contract) about 25-30% of historical $50K evaluations passed; at 3 MNQ ($117 a contract) about 45-55%, because the stop has room and four losers no longer eat the $2,000 drawdown. Once funded, tick it.")
account  = funded ? "Funded" : "Evaluation"
evalQty  = input.int(1, "Contracts in an evaluation", minval = 1, maxval = 60, group = grpT)
fundQty  = input.int(1, "Contracts on a funded account", minval = 1, maxval = 60, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "Every figure in docs/RESULTS.md is per contract. What matters is the max loss per contract (the dashboard shows it): $350 over 10 contracts is $35 a contract, a 17.5-point stop; over 3 it is $117, 58 points. See docs/RESULTS.md, rounds thirteen, twenty-seven, thirty-two and thirty-seven.")
qty = account == "Evaluation" ? evalQty : fundQty
maxLoss  = input.float(260, "Max loss per trade, $ (all contracts, 0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 10, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "A second stop this many dollars from the entry fill, for the whole position, live from the fill like a bracket order; whichever of it and the line stop is closer is used. Spread over many contracts it gets tight: $350 over 10 contracts is a $35 stop each, which normal 5-minute moves hit, and on 2023-2026 it made about $6 a day per contract against about $20 at $117 each. On 16 years, caps of $100-$200 per contract raised profit per day in every period and cut the worst losing stretch. Fees, slippage and a gap through the stop can add to the loss.")
afterQty = input.int(0, "After a losing trade: contracts (0 = the same)", minval = 0, maxval = 60, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "The trade after a losing trade uses this many contracts and the max loss below, so its stop sits further away (v2.8: the same 4 MNQ and $1,000, 125 points, against 93.75 for 4 MNQ and $750; v2.6 was 9 MNQ and $1,500 against 10 and $750). A winner, or the next trade, goes back to the normal size. Ordinary noise stopped many re-entries after a loss; the wider stop turned some of them into winners: back-to-back losers 36% against 42% of losers on the user's MNQ window, 51% against 57% on NQ futures 2015-2025 (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.1). It risks up to $1,000 on that trade, and never more than what is left of the day's loss limit.")
lastEntry = input.string("15:00", "Last check for new entries", options = ["15:00", "15:30"], group = grpT,
     tooltip = "v2.2: no new entries from the 15:30 check. With 25 minutes left before the 15:55 exit such a trade can't reach its take-profit but can lose its full stop: at v2.1's settings the 15:30 entries lost on average on NQ futures 2015-2025 (258 trades, -$58 each), the index 2011-2026 (370, -$53) and the user's MNQ window; without them +4% net on NQ, +3% on the index, +5% on the window (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.2).")
lastEntryEnd = lastEntry == "15:00" ? 900 : 930
bigDayK = input.float(1.5, "After a big day: no trades its way if its range > this x the average (0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 0.05, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "v2.3: after a session whose 09:30-16:00 range was over this many times the average range of the last sessions below (that session included), no new entries the next day in that session's direction (its close against its open); the other direction trades as usual. After an outsized day the next session tends to retrace: at v2.2's settings the next day's trades in the big day's direction lost on average on NQ futures 2015-2025 (365 trades, -$112 each) and the Nasdaq-100 index 2011-2026 (536, -$67), while those against it made +$148 and +$190. With the rule, NQ futures +14% net and +39% net per drawdown, better in both halves and 8 of 11 years; the index +10% and +15%, 12 of 16 years (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.3).")
bigDayN = input.int(10, "After a big day: sessions in the average range", minval = 2, maxval = 60, group = grpT)
calmK = input.float(0.7, "Calm stretch: no trades if the recent average range < this x the longer one (0 = off)", minval = 0, maxval = 2, step = 0.05, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "v2.5: no new entries (nor heads-ups) on a day when the average 09:30-16:00 range of the last sessions (the first number below) is under this share of the average over the longer stretch (the second). When ranges have shrunk well below normal, breakouts of the noise area mostly fail: at v2.4's settings trades after such stretches made the least of any fifth of days on NQ futures 2015-2025, the Nasdaq-100 index 2011-2026 and the 2025-2026 stand-in. With the rule, the profit factor rose on all three, on both 5- and 30-minute bars, at every pair of lengths tried (5-20 against 40-100 sessions), with net level on the histories (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.5).")
calmShort = input.int(10, "Calm stretch: recent sessions", minval = 2, maxval = 50, group = grpT)
calmLong = input.int(40, "Calm stretch: longer stretch, sessions", minval = 5, maxval = 100, group = grpT)
dailyLimit = input.float(900, "Max loss a day, $ (0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 50, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "v2.7: no trade may risk more than what is left of this loss today (today's closed P/L counted, wins add room back). A trade that would risk more takes fewer contracts with the same stop distance; when not even 1 contract fits, no new entries until tomorrow. Trading never stops just because of a loss: the next trade is smaller instead. The stop is a resting order, so a gap or fast market through it can still lose a little more (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.7).")
trailDD = input.float(0, "Trailing drawdown (end of day), $ (0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 100, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "v3.0: a prop firm's end-of-day trailing drawdown. The floor is your highest end-of-day balance minus this; no trade may risk more than what is left above it (fewer contracts, the same stop; none when not even 1 fits). With the $1,000 a day limit, a trade gets the smaller of the two rooms (docs/RESULTS.md, v3.0).")
trailStop = input.bool(true, "Trailing drawdown stops at the starting balance", group = grpT,
     tooltip = "As at most prop firms: once the floor reaches your starting balance it stays there. Unticked, it keeps trailing your highest end-of-day balance for ever.")
trailFrom = input.int(20250102, "Trailing drawdown and contract steps from date, YYYYMMDD (0 = the first bar)", minval = 0, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "The day the account started: 20250102 (the default) for the backtest from January 2, 2025; for a live account, the day it began. Before it the script trades the starting contracts with no trailing drawdown, so the steps and the floor count only from this day.")
profitStep = input.float(0, "Add a contract per $ of profit (0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 100, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "v3.0: one more contract for each this much closed profit since the start date (the same stop distance and max loss per contract), up to the most contracts below. A $2,000 trailing drawdown fits about 1 MNQ until there is a cushion: at 1 MNQ the 2025-2026 stand-in's worst end-of-day drawdown was $1,841. v3.4: $2,500 (v3.3's $1,500 made no more on the user's chart). With v3.1's trend rule, steps of $1,500-2,500 never touched the floor on any test set; $1,000 got stuck on the histories (docs/RESULTS.md, v3.0-v3.3).")
sizeUpTo = input.int(15, "Most contracts (0 = no limit)", minval = 0, maxval = 60, group = grpT)
budgetStop = input.bool(false, "Size by the trade's own stop", group = grpT,
     tooltip = "v3.0: a contract's risk for the loss limits is its stop at entry, the line stop or the max loss, whichever is closer (plus fees and a tick each way). Unticked: always the full max loss.")
trendN = input.int(50, "No shorts while the last close is above its average of this many sessions (0 = off)", minval = 0, maxval = 250, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "v3.1: in an uptrend (yesterday's 16:00 close above the average of the last 50 sessions' closes) no new shorts; longs as usual. On the user's TradingView chart 1/2025-12/2025 v3.0's shorts lost $2,179 while its longs made $2,117; shorts against the 50-session trend lost on NQ futures 2015-2025 and the Nasdaq-100 index 2011-2026 too (docs/RESULTS.md, v3.1).")
squeezeMin = input.float(20, "Never stuck: when no contract fits, 1 with its stop cut to the room left, if at least this many points (0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 5, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "v3.1: near the trailing floor (or the day's limit) not even 1 contract may fit; v3.0 then stopped trading, on the user's chart for most of 2026. Now it takes 1 MNQ with its max loss cut to the room left (less costs), as long as that leaves a stop of at least this many points.")
rangePos = input.float(0.65, "Entries near the day's extreme: the close in the top this share of the day's range (0 = off)", minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "v2.9: a long needs the check's close in the top part of the day's 09:30-to-now range: (close - day low) / (day high - day low) at least this (a short: the bottom part, (day high - close) / (day high - day low)). A breakout of the noise area after the day had already run further and come back down to the line made about nothing: profit factor 1.0-1.1 on NQ futures 2015-2025, the Nasdaq-100 index 2011-2026 and the 2025-2026 stand-in, against 1.5 for the rest. Skipping them frees the day's loss room for the others (docs/RESULTS.md, v2.9).")
afterMaxLoss = input.float(0, "After a losing trade: max loss per trade, $ (0 = the same)", minval = 0, step = 10, group = grpT)
skipDates = input.string("2025-01-01,2025-01-09,2025-01-20,2025-02-17,2025-04-18,2025-05-26,2025-06-19,2025-07-03,2025-07-04,2025-09-01,2025-11-27,2025-11-28,2025-12-24,2025-12-25,2026-01-01,2026-01-19,2026-02-16,2026-04-03,2026-05-25,2026-06-19,2026-07-03,2026-09-07,2026-11-26,2026-11-27,2026-12-24,2026-12-25,2027-01-01,2027-01-18,2027-02-15,2027-03-26,2027-05-31,2027-06-18,2027-07-05,2027-09-06,2027-11-25,2027-11-26,2027-12-24",
     "Don't trade on these dates", group = grpT,
     tooltip = "YYYY-MM-DD, comma separated. Pre-filled with the 2025-2027 US market holidays and half days (2025 for backtests from January 2025), when MNQ trades a short session. Add news days if you like.")
fedNoShorts = input.bool(true, "Fed days: no shorts before 14:00", group = grpT,
     tooltip = "On scheduled Fed announcement days, skip short signals from the checks before the 14:00 statement (10:00-13:30); longs and everything after 14:00 as usual. Stocks tend to drift up into the announcement (Lucca & Moench, 2015). Tested before running on 2011-2018, then 2019-2022 and 2023-2026: a little more per day in every period and the same worst losing stretch. It changes only 1-3 trades a year. See docs/RESULTS.md, round twenty-four.")
fedDates = input.string("2025-01-29,2025-03-19,2025-05-07,2025-06-18,2025-07-30,2025-09-17,2025-10-29,2025-12-10,2026-01-28,2026-03-18,2026-04-29,2026-06-17,2026-07-29,2026-09-16,2026-10-28,2026-12-09,2027-01-27,2027-03-17,2027-04-28,2027-06-09,2027-07-28,2027-09-15,2027-10-27,2027-12-08",
     "Fed announcement days", group = grpT,
     tooltip = "YYYY-MM-DD, comma separated: the scheduled FOMC statement days from federalreserve.gov, 2025-2027. In 2028, add that year's dates.")
exitMode = input.string("Resting stop at the line", "Exit", options = ["Resting stop at the line", "Half-hour check"], group = grpT,
     tooltip = "Resting stop: once in a trade, a stop order sits at the noise line and moves with it at every half hour. Tested on 16 years: smaller worst days and better evaluation odds. Half-hour check: the paper's rule, exit only when a half-hour check closes back inside the lines.")
useStop = exitMode == "Resting stop at the line"
stopBuf = input.float(0.24, "Stop distance past the line, in noise units", minval = 0, maxval = 2, step = 0.01, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "0 puts the stop exactly on the line. 0.24 is how far price typically overshoots the line before resuming, measured on 2011-2018; it cut whipsaw stop-outs and raised profit per day on every later period. See docs/RESULTS.md.")
tpUnits = input.float(2.0, "Take profit, noise units from the entry (0 = off)", minval = 0, maxval = 10, step = 0.1, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "A limit order this many noise units past your fill (1.5 x the current noise x the fill price), working from the bar after the fill; with the resting stop only. Chosen walk-forward, each year from the years before only: over 2015-2026 it raised profit per day from $24.66 to $25.77 per contract, the t-stat from 4.71 to 5.39, cut the worst losing stretch from $5,178 to $4,185, and raised the $50K pass rate at 2 MNQ in 2023-2026 from 42% to 68%. See docs/RESULTS.md, round twenty-six.")
lockAt = input.float(0.35, "Lock a small win: trigger, in max losses (0 = off)", minval = 0, maxval = 10, step = 0.05, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "Once a trade has been this far in profit (1 = as far as the max loss: 17.5 points with $350 on 10 MNQ), the stop moves to the entry plus the points below, so the trade can't turn into a loser. Like Tradovate's Auto Breakeven: set the trigger and the offset in your bracket (70 and +10 ticks at the defaults). Tested at $35 a contract on 1-minute data, 2011-2026 index and 2015-2025 NQ futures: winners from about 14% to 48%, the same money, a higher t-stat (docs/RESULTS.md, round thirty-seven). On a 5-minute chart the lock moves one bar after the trigger is touched, so the chart's backtest shows fewer winners than the broker gets: over 16 years at 10 MNQ and $350, about 40% on this chart against about 49% with Tradovate's Auto Breakeven (docs/RESULTS.md).")
lockPlus = input.float(2.5, "Lock: stop to the entry plus, points", minval = 0, maxval = 50, step = 0.25, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "2.5 points is $5 a contract, more than the round-trip fees and a tick of slippage, so a locked trade closes as a small winner.")
tightenOnly = input.bool(true, "Stop only ever tightens", group = grpT,
     tooltip = "In a trade the stop never moves back toward the price: when the noise line steps back (it does in about 3 of 10 half-hour steps), the stop stays where it was. Adopted in the NinjaTrader strategy in round one hundred and thirty-nine: more net in all four test periods with a slightly smaller drawdown. Webhook orders always use it.")
maxLosers = input.int(0, "Max losing trades a day (0 = no limit)", minval = 0, maxval = 20, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "After this many losing trades in a day, no new entries until tomorrow (an open trade runs on as usual). Tested before running at 10 MNQ and $350 with the lock, on 1-minute data: on 2011-2018, 2019-2022, 2023-2026 and NQ futures 2015-2025 it made more per day, with a higher t-stat and a smaller worst losing stretch (31% smaller on NQ futures). 1 or 2 losers cut the profit by a third or more: the winner often comes after a few stop-outs. See docs/RESULTS.md, round thirty-eight.")
timeStop = input.int(0, "Time stop: close a losing trade not yet locked this many minutes after its fill (0 = off)", minval = 0, maxval = 390, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "At a bar close this many minutes or more after the fill, a trade that is losing and has not reached the lock is closed at market (it fills at the next bar's open). 60 in funded growth mode: tested before running in docs/NINJATRADER_V38.md (G6), more net on all three 5-minute sets with the floor never touched. Not tested in the evaluation, so 0 (off) there.")
grpV = "Display"
showBands = input.bool(true, "Show noise area", group = grpV)
showLabels = input.bool(true, "Show BUY / SELL / EXIT labels", group = grpV)
shadeTrades = input.bool(true, "Shade the chart while in a trade", group = grpV)
showDash  = input.bool(true, "Show dashboard", group = grpV)
showLog   = input.bool(true, "Show trade log", group = grpV,
     tooltip = "A table at the bottom right with every trade the bot took, newest first: the time it opened and closed (New York, month-day hour:minute), side and contracts, entry and exit prices, P/L after fees, and why it closed. The open trade, if any, is on top.")
logRows   = input.int(10, "Trades in the log", minval = 1, maxval = 30, group = grpV)
grpE = "Evaluation tracker"
evalStart = input.int(0, "Evaluation start date, YYYYMMDD (0 = off)", minval = 0, group = grpE,
     tooltip = "The day your evaluation began, e.g. 20261020. A table at the bottom left then follows it from the strategy's trades since that day, by the rules below (end-of-day balances): profit toward the target, the trailing drawdown floor and how many full losers fit above it, your best day against the consistency rule, and what it takes to pass. It reads the trades only; it changes nothing.")
evalTarget = input.float(3000, "Profit target, $", minval = 0, step = 100, group = grpE)
evalDD = input.float(2000, "End-of-day trailing drawdown, $", minval = 0, step = 100, group = grpE,
     tooltip = "Trails the highest end-of-day balance and stops rising at the starting balance, as the backtests in docs/RESULTS.md assume.")
evalCons = input.float(50, "Best day under this % of the profit (0 = no rule)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = grpE)
evalDays = input.int(5, "Minimum trading days", minval = 0, group = grpE)
grpA = "Automation"
hookMode = input.string("Off", "Webhook orders", options = ["Off", "TradersPost"], group = grpA,
     tooltip = "TradersPost: every order this strategy fills also carries a TradersPost JSON message (entry with its stop and take-profit attached, and exit), so an alert can place the trades at your broker within seconds. Each minute of delay cost about 15-25% of the profit on 1-minute data (docs/RESULTS.md, round thirty-five). In this mode the stop only ever tightens during a trade, so the broker's stop, placed with the entry, is never tighter than the one on the chart; tested, it made the same money. Check your prop firm allows automation first: Take Profit Trader, Apex and others do not. Setup in docs/NOISE.md.")
hookTicker = input.string("", "Contract for the webhook (blank = the chart's)", group = grpA,
     tooltip = "The exact contract, e.g. MNQZ2026. Blank uses the contract behind the chart (MNQ1! -> the current front month). Update it at each quarterly roll if you type one in.")
useHook = hookMode == "TradersPost"

// ── Clock
barMin  = int(timeframe.in_seconds() / 60)
validTf = barMin >= 1 and 30 % barMin == 0
tMin    = hour(time, TZ) * 60 + minute(time, TZ)
endMin  = tMin + barMin   // bar close, minutes after midnight
inRth   = tMin >= RTH_OPEN and endMin <= RTH_CLOSE
isCheck = validTf and inRth and endMin >= FIRST_CHECK and endMin <= LAST_CHECK and (endMin - FIRST_CHECK) % 30 == 0

hhmmText(int mins) => str.tostring(int(mins / 60)) + ":" + (mins % 60 < 10 ? "0" : "") + str.tostring(mins % 60)
px(float x) => str.tostring(x, format.mintick)
// every alert() goes through here: once per bar close
say(string msg) =>
    alert(msg, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
// ── Webhook messages (TradersPost JSON), sent with order fills when "Webhook orders" is on
hookSym = hookTicker != "" ? hookTicker : na(syminfo.current_contract) ? syminfo.ticker : syminfo.current_contract
jsonEntry(string action, float est, float stop, float tp, int q) =>
    '{"ticker": "' + hookSym + '", "action": "' + action + '", "orderType": "market", "quantity": ' + str.tostring(q) + ', "price": ' + px(est) +
         (na(stop) ? '' : ', "stopLoss": {"type": "stop", "stopPrice": ' + px(stop) + '}') +
         (na(tp) ? '' : ', "takeProfit": {"limitPrice": ' + px(tp) + '}') + '}'
jsonExit = '{"ticker": "' + hookSym + '", "action": "exit", "cancel": true}'
hookExit = useHook ? jsonExit : ""
usd(float x) => (x < 0 ? "-$" : "$") + str.tostring(math.abs(x), "#,##0.00")
stamp(int t) => str.format_time(t, "MM-dd HH:mm", TZ)   // New York time, month-day hour:minute
why(string c) => c == "Back inside" ? (useStop ? "stop at the line" : "back inside at a check") : c == "Max loss" ? "max loss stop" : c == "Lock" ? "locked win" : c == "Target" ? "take profit" : c == "16:00 close" ? "16:00 close" : c == "Session ended" ? "session ended" : c == "Time stop" ? "time stop" : str.contains(c, "Reverse") ? "reversed" : c
// Losing trades closed since closed-trade number `first` (today's: from the count at 09:30), for the daily limit
losersSince(int first) =>
    int n = 0
    if strategy.closedtrades > first
        for j = first to strategy.closedtrades - 1
            if strategy.closedtrades.profit(j) < 0 and strategy.closedtrades.exit_comment(j) != "Session ended"
                n += 1
    n
// A signal label on the candle that triggered it: below the candle for buys, above for sells.
mark(string txt, bool below, color c) =>
    if showLabels
        label.new(bar_index, below ? low : high, txt, yloc = below ? yloc.belowbar : yloc.abovebar,
             style = below ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = c, textcolor = color.white, size = size.normal)

// ── State
var float dayOpen = na
var float prevClose = na
var float lastRthClose = na
var float ub = na
var float lb = na
var float sig = na   // this check's noise (sigma), which sets the stop distance
var moves = array.new_float(lookback * N_CHECKS, na)   // ring buffer: one row of 12 moves per session
var today = array.new_float(N_CHECKS, na)
var int filled = 0
var int slot = 0
var bool skipToday = false
var bool fedToday = false
var string lastSignal = "-"
var int prevClosed = 0   // closed trades at the end of the previous bar
var float dayStartNet = 0.0   // strategy.netprofit at 09:30, for today's P/L
var int dayStartClosed = 0    // strategy.closedtrades at 09:30, for today's trade count

// ── Losing trades in a row (v2.1): a winner resets the count; a trade closed because the session ended doesn't count.
// The next entry after a loser uses the after-loss contracts and max loss (a wider stop); tQty / tMaxLoss are the open
// (or just placed) trade's.
var int lossRun = 0
var int lossSeen = 0
if strategy.closedtrades > lossSeen
    for j = lossSeen to strategy.closedtrades - 1
        pj = strategy.closedtrades.profit(j)
        if pj < 0 and strategy.closedtrades.exit_comment(j) != "Session ended"
            lossRun += 1
        else if pj >= 0
            lossRun := 0
    lossSeen := strategy.closedtrades
afterLoss = lossRun > 0
qBase0 = afterLoss and afterQty > 0 ? afterQty : qty
mlBase0 = afterLoss and afterMaxLoss > 0 ? afterMaxLoss : maxLoss
// v3.0: the end-of-day trailing drawdown. At each session's first bar (yesterday's end-of-day balance), from trailFrom
var float trailBase = na
var float trailPeak = na
if trailDD > 0 and tMin == RTH_OPEN and (trailFrom <= 0 or year(time, TZ) * 10000 + month(time, TZ) * 100 + dayofmonth(time, TZ) >= trailFrom)
    if na(trailBase)
        trailBase := strategy.netprofit
        trailPeak := strategy.netprofit
    trailPeak := math.max(trailPeak, strategy.netprofit)
// v3.0: a contract more for each profitStep of closed profit since then, up to sizeUpTo (the same max loss per contract)
qBase = qBase0
mlBase = mlBase0
if profitStep > 0 and not na(trailBase)
    qUp = qBase0 + int(math.floor(math.max(0.0, strategy.netprofit - trailBase) / profitStep))
    qUp := sizeUpTo > 0 ? math.min(qUp, sizeUpTo) : qUp
    mlBase := mlBase0 / qBase0 * qUp
    qBase := qUp
// v2.7: today's loss budget, and since v3.0 the room above the trailing floor: a new trade gets the smaller. Each
// contract can lose its max loss plus costs (fees both ways, a tick of slippage each way)
dayPnlNow = strategy.netprofit - dayStartNet
trailFloor = na(trailPeak) ? na : trailStop ? math.min(trailPeak - trailDD, trailBase) : trailPeak - trailDD
roomDay = dailyLimit > 0 ? dailyLimit + dayPnlNow : na
roomTrail = trailDD > 0 and not na(trailFloor) ? strategy.netprofit - trailFloor : na
moneyRoom = na(roomDay) ? roomTrail : na(roomTrail) ? roomDay : math.min(roomDay, roomTrail)
budgetOn = (dailyLimit > 0 or trailDD > 0) and mlBase > 0
costC = 2 * 0.62 + 2 * syminfo.mintick * syminfo.pointvalue
perC = budgetOn ? mlBase / qBase + costC : 0.0
fitQ = budgetOn and not na(moneyRoom) ? math.floor(moneyRoom / perC + 1e-9) : qBase
budgetOk = fitQ >= 1
qNext = budgetOk and fitQ < qBase ? fitQ : qBase
mlNext = qNext < qBase ? mlBase / qBase * qNext : mlBase
// The contracts for an entry whose stop at the fill is stopPts away (budgetStop: its own stop, else the max loss)
qFor(float stopPts) =>
    int q = budgetOk ? qNext : 0
    if budgetOn and not na(moneyRoom) and budgetStop and useStop
        pc = math.min(stopPts, mlBase / qBase / syminfo.pointvalue) * syminfo.pointvalue + costC
        f = math.floor(moneyRoom / pc + 1e-9)
        q := f < qBase ? f : qBase
    q
var int tQty = 0
var float tMaxLoss = 0.0

// ── The resting stop filled during this bar (the broker did it; show it). A trade can open and
// close inside one bar, so look at the closed-trade count, not the position.
lastTrade = strategy.closedtrades - 1
lastWhy = strategy.closedtrades > 0 ? strategy.closedtrades.exit_comment(lastTrade) : ""
stopFired = useStop and strategy.closedtrades > prevClosed and (lastWhy == "Back inside" or lastWhy == "Max loss" or lastWhy == "Lock" or lastWhy == "Target")
if stopFired
    side = strategy.closedtrades.size(lastTrade) > 0 ? "LONG" : "SHORT"
    exitPx = px(strategy.closedtrades.exit_price(lastTrade))
    if lastWhy == "Target"
        mark("TARGET", strategy.closedtrades.size(lastTrade) < 0, color.teal)
        lastSignal := "TARGET hit @ " + exitPx
        if useHook   // the order-fill alert carries the webhook message; this one is for your phone
            say("TARGET: the " + str.lower(side) + " reached the take-profit at " + exitPx + ". The webhook closed it.")
    else
        mark("EXIT", strategy.closedtrades.size(lastTrade) < 0, color.gray)
        lastSignal := "EXIT (" + (lastWhy == "Max loss" ? "max loss" : lastWhy == "Lock" ? "locked win" : "line touched") + ") @ " + exitPx
        if useHook
            say("EXIT " + side + ": price hit the stop at " + exitPx + ". The webhook closed it.")

// ── Today's baseline for the dashboard, taken at 09:30 before anything else happens this bar
if tMin == RTH_OPEN
    dayStartNet := strategy.netprofit
    dayStartClosed := strategy.closedtrades

// ── A session that ended early (half day, data gap): get flat
if strategy.position_size != 0 and (not inRth or tMin == RTH_OPEN)
    mark("EXIT NOW", strategy.position_size < 0, color.orange)
    lastSignal := "EXIT NOW (session ended)"
    strategy.close_all(comment = "Session ended", alert_message = hookExit, immediately = true)
    say("EXIT NOW: the session ended with a position open. Close your MNQ position at market.")

// ── After a big day (v2.3): each completed session's 09:30-16:00 range (as a share of its open) and direction; at 09:30
// the side not to trade today, if yesterday's range was over bigDayK x the average of the last bigDayN
var dayRanges = array.new_float(0)
var dayDirs = array.new_int(0)
var float dayHi = na
var float dayLo = na
var int blockDir = 0
var bool calmDay = false  // v2.5: today follows a calm stretch, no new entries
var dayCloses = array.new_float(0)  // v3.1: completed sessions' 16:00 closes
var int trendDir = 0  // v3.1: yesterday's close against the trendN-session average: 1 above, -1 below

// ── New day at the 09:30 bar
if tMin == RTH_OPEN
    blockDir := 0
    nR = array.size(dayRanges)
    if bigDayK > 0 and nR >= bigDayN
        float sR = 0.0
        for j = nR - bigDayN to nR - 1
            sR += array.get(dayRanges, j)
        if array.get(dayRanges, nR - 1) > bigDayK * (sR / bigDayN)
            blockDir := array.get(dayDirs, nR - 1)
    nC = array.size(dayCloses)
    if trendN > 0 and nC >= trendN
        float sC = 0.0
        for j = nC - trendN to nC - 1
            sC += array.get(dayCloses, j)
        lastC = array.get(dayCloses, nC - 1)
        trendDir := lastC > sC / trendN ? 1 : lastC < sC / trendN ? -1 : 0
    calmDay := false
    if calmK > 0 and nR >= calmLong
        float sS = 0.0
        float sL = 0.0
        for j = nR - calmLong to nR - 1
            sL += array.get(dayRanges, j)
            if j >= nR - calmShort
                sS += array.get(dayRanges, j)
        calmDay := sS / calmShort < calmK * (sL / calmLong)
    dayHi := na
    dayLo := na
    prevClose := lastRthClose
    dayOpen := open
    ub := na
    lb := na
    sig := na
    skipToday := str.contains(skipDates, str.format_time(time, "yyyy-MM-dd", TZ))
    fedToday := fedNoShorts and str.contains(fedDates, str.format_time(time, "yyyy-MM-dd", TZ))
    for k = 0 to N_CHECKS - 1
        array.set(today, k, na)
if inRth
    lastRthClose := close
    dayHi := na(dayHi) ? high : math.max(dayHi, high)
    dayLo := na(dayLo) ? low : math.min(dayLo, low)
// Overnight bars on the chart (an ETH session): the dashboard suggests RTH, which loads about 4x more days
var bool sawOvernight = false
if tMin < RTH_OPEN or tMin >= RTH_CLOSE + 15
    sawOvernight := true

// v2.9: is the close near the day's extreme on side d (rangePos)?
rangeOk(int d) =>
    rng = dayHi - dayLo
    rangePos <= 0 or na(rng) or rng <= 0 or (d > 0 ? (close - dayLo) / rng : (dayHi - close) / rng) >= rangePos

// ── Half-hour checks
longPlaced = false
shortPlaced = false
var int qPlaced = 0   // the contracts of the entry placed at this check
var float mlPlaced = 0.0   // and its max loss
if isCheck and not na(dayOpen)
    k = int((endMin - FIRST_CHECK) / 30)
    array.set(today, k, math.abs(close / dayOpen - 1))
    if filled >= lookback and not na(prevClose)
        float s = 0.0
        for d = 0 to lookback - 1
            s += array.get(moves, d * N_CHECKS + k)
        sigma = s / lookback
        sig := sigma
        ub := math.max(dayOpen, prevClose) * (1 + sigma)
        lb := math.min(dayOpen, prevClose) * (1 - sigma)
        nextCheck = k == N_CHECKS - 1 ? "the 16:00 close" : hhmmText(endMin + 30)
        longStopNow = ub * (1 - stopBuf * sig)
        shortStopNow = lb * (1 + stopBuf * sig)
        // The bracket to place with the entry, from the expected fill (this close plus a tick): the stop is the closer of
        // the line stop and the max loss, the target tpUnits noise units away. Same numbers the backtest uses.
        estL = close + syminfo.mintick
        estS = close - syminfo.mintick
        qL0 = qFor(estL - longStopNow)   // v3.0: the contracts the loss limits leave for a long / a short now
        qS0 = qFor(shortStopNow - estS)
        // v3.1: when not one fits, 1 contract with its max loss cut to the room left (squeezeMin points at least)
        sqzOk = squeezeMin > 0 and budgetOn and not na(moneyRoom) and moneyRoom - costC >= squeezeMin * syminfo.pointvalue
        qL = qL0 < 1 and sqzOk ? 1 : qL0
        qS = qS0 < 1 and sqzOk ? 1 : qS0
        mlL = qL0 < 1 and sqzOk ? moneyRoom - costC : mlBase / qBase * qL
        mlS = qS0 < 1 and sqzOk ? moneyRoom - costC : mlBase / qBase * qS
        capPtsL = mlBase > 0 and qL > 0 ? mlL / qL / syminfo.pointvalue : na
        capPtsS = mlBase > 0 and qS > 0 ? mlS / qS / syminfo.pointvalue : na
        bracketL = na(capPtsL) ? longStopNow : math.max(longStopNow, estL - capPtsL)
        bracketS = na(capPtsS) ? shortStopNow : math.min(shortStopNow, estS + capPtsS)
        whyL = bracketL > longStopNow ? "your " + usd(mlL) + " max loss" : "just below the upper line"
        whyS = bracketS < shortStopNow ? "your " + usd(mlS) + " max loss" : "just above the lower line"
        tpTextL = tpUnits > 0 ? ", take-profit limit " + px(estL * (1 + tpUnits * sig)) : ""
        tpTextS = tpUnits > 0 ? ", take-profit limit " + px(estS * (1 - tpUnits * sig)) : ""
        tpL = useStop and tpUnits > 0 ? estL * (1 + tpUnits * sig) : na
        tpS = useStop and tpUnits > 0 ? estS * (1 - tpUnits * sig) : na
        lockPtsL = useStop and lockAt > 0 and not na(capPtsL) ? lockAt * capPtsL : na
        lockPtsS = useStop and lockAt > 0 and not na(capPtsS) ? lockAt * capPtsS : na
        lockTextL = na(lockPtsL) ? "" : " Auto-breakeven: at " + px(estL + lockPtsL) + " move the stop to " + px(estL + lockPlus) + "."
        lockTextS = na(lockPtsS) ? "" : " Auto-breakeven: at " + px(estS - lockPtsS) + " move the stop to " + px(estS - lockPlus) + "."
        moveText = " If your fill is different, keep the same distances. At each half hour move the stop with the line (the dashboard shows it); the max loss never moves."
        // When the max loss is the closer stop (always at 10 MNQ and $350), the line decided under 1 trade in 100 over
        // 16 years and a bracket left alone made the same money (docs/RESULTS.md): one bracket, no stop moves.
        keepText = " If your fill is different, keep the same distances. Leave the stop there: the line almost never comes closer than your max loss."
        holdLong = useStop ? "Bracket: stop " + px(bracketL) + " (" + whyL + ")" + tpTextL + ", for a fill near " + px(estL) + "." + lockTextL + (bracketL > longStopNow ? keepText : moveText) :
             "Hold until a half-hour check closes back below the upper line, or the 16:00 close."
        holdShort = useStop ? "Bracket: stop " + px(bracketS) + " (" + whyS + ")" + tpTextS + ", for a fill near " + px(estS) + "." + lockTextS + (bracketS < shortStopNow ? keepText : moveText) :
             "Hold until a half-hour check closes back above the lower line, or the 16:00 close."
        pos = strategy.position_size
        inPosStop = useStop and pos != 0   // exits are the resting stop's job
        shortOk = not (fedToday and endMin < FED_CUTOFF)   // Fed day: no shorts before the 14:00 statement
        freshOk = maxLosers <= 0 or losersSince(dayStartClosed) < maxLosers   // the daily limit on new entries
        if not skipToday
            if not inPosStop and pos > 0 and close < ub
                if close < lb and shortOk
                    strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qNext, comment = "Reverse short", alert_message = useHook ? jsonEntry("sell", estS, na, na, qNext) : "")
                    mark("REVERSE\nSELL " + str.tostring(2 * qNext), false, color.red)
                    lastSignal := "REVERSE to short " + hhmmText(endMin) + " @ " + px(close)
                    say("REVERSE: exit the long and SELL " + str.tostring(qNext) + " MNQ at market now. Price " + px(close) +
                         " is below the noise area (lower " + px(lb) + "). Next check " + nextCheck + ".")
                else
                    strategy.close("Long", comment = "Back inside", alert_message = hookExit)
                    mark("EXIT", false, color.gray)
                    lastSignal := "EXIT long " + hhmmText(endMin) + " @ " + px(close)
                    say("EXIT LONG at market now. Price " + px(close) + " closed back below the upper line (" + px(ub) +
                         "). Stay flat until the next signal.")
            else if not inPosStop and pos < 0 and close > lb
                if close > ub
                    strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qNext, comment = "Reverse long", alert_message = useHook ? jsonEntry("buy", estL, na, na, qNext) : "")
                    mark("REVERSE\nBUY " + str.tostring(2 * qNext), true, color.green)
                    lastSignal := "REVERSE to long " + hhmmText(endMin) + " @ " + px(close)
                    say("REVERSE: exit the short and BUY " + str.tostring(qNext) + " MNQ at market now. Price " + px(close) +
                         " is above the noise area (upper " + px(ub) + "). Next check " + nextCheck + ".")
                else
                    strategy.close("Short", comment = "Back inside", alert_message = hookExit)
                    mark("EXIT", true, color.gray)
                    lastSignal := "EXIT short " + hhmmText(endMin) + " @ " + px(close)
                    say("EXIT SHORT at market now. Price " + px(close) + " closed back above the lower line (" + px(lb) +
                         "). Stay flat until the next signal.")
            else if pos == 0 and close > ub and freshOk and endMin <= lastEntryEnd and blockDir != 1 and not calmDay and qL >= 1 and rangeOk(1)
                strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qL, comment = "Above noise",
                     alert_message = useHook ? jsonEntry("buy", estL, useStop ? bracketL : na, tpL, qL) : "")
                longPlaced := true
                qPlaced := qL
                mlPlaced := mlL
                mark("BUY " + str.tostring(qL) + " MNQ", true, color.green)
                lastSignal := "BUY " + hhmmText(endMin) + " @ " + px(close)
                say("BUY " + str.tostring(qL) + " MNQ at market now. Price " + px(close) + " is above the noise area (upper " +
                     px(ub) + "). " + holdLong + " Next check " + nextCheck + ".")
            else if pos == 0 and close < lb and shortOk and freshOk and endMin <= lastEntryEnd and blockDir != -1 and not calmDay and qS >= 1 and rangeOk(-1) and not (trendN > 0 and trendDir == 1)
                strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qS, comment = "Below noise",
                     alert_message = useHook ? jsonEntry("sell", estS, useStop ? bracketS : na, tpS, qS) : "")
                shortPlaced := true
                qPlaced := qS
                mlPlaced := mlS
                mark("SELL " + str.tostring(qS) + " MNQ", false, color.red)
                lastSignal := "SELL " + hhmmText(endMin) + " @ " + px(close)
                say("SELL " + str.tostring(qS) + " MNQ at market now. Price " + px(close) + " is below the noise area (lower " +
                     px(lb) + "). " + holdShort + " Next check " + nextCheck + ".")

// ── Heads-up: five minutes before a check, flat, and price already past that check's line. On 2011-2018 a signal
// followed about 9 times in 10, and 9 signals in 10 had one: time to have the order ready (each minute of delay cost
// 15-25% of the profit, docs/RESULTS.md round thirty-five). Alerts only; it changes no trade.
var string headsUp = ""
preEnd = endMin + 5
if isCheck
    headsUp := ""
if validTf and 5 % barMin == 0 and inRth and preEnd >= FIRST_CHECK and preEnd <= math.min(LAST_CHECK, lastEntryEnd) and (preEnd - FIRST_CHECK) % 30 == 0 and not na(dayOpen) and filled >= lookback and not na(prevClose) and strategy.position_size == 0 and not skipToday and not calmDay and budgetOk and (maxLosers <= 0 or losersSince(dayStartClosed) < maxLosers)
    kh = int((preEnd - FIRST_CHECK) / 30)
    float sh = 0.0
    for d = 0 to lookback - 1
        sh += array.get(moves, d * N_CHECKS + kh)
    sgh = sh / lookback
    upH = math.max(dayOpen, prevClose) * (1 + sgh)
    loH = math.min(dayOpen, prevClose) * (1 - sgh)
    lockH = useStop and lockAt > 0 and mlNext > 0 ? ", auto-breakeven at +" + px(lockAt * mlNext / qNext / syminfo.pointvalue) + " to +" + px(lockPlus) : ""
    readyH = " Get the order ready: " + str.tostring(qNext) + " MNQ, stop " + (mlNext > 0 ? px(mlNext / qNext / syminfo.pointvalue) + " points from your fill (your " + usd(mlNext) + ")" : "at the line") + (useStop and tpUnits > 0 ? ", take-profit about " + px(tpUnits * sgh * close) + " points" : "") + lockH + "."
    if close > upH
        if blockDir != 1
            headsUp := hhmmText(preEnd) + " BUY likely"
            say("HEADS-UP: " + hhmmText(preEnd) + " BUY likely. Price " + px(close) + " is already above the " + hhmmText(preEnd) + " upper line (" + px(upH) + ")." + readyH)
    else if close < loH and not (fedToday and preEnd < FED_CUTOFF)
        if blockDir != -1
            headsUp := hhmmText(preEnd) + " SELL likely"
            say("HEADS-UP: " + hhmmText(preEnd) + " SELL likely. Price " + px(close) + " is already below the " + hhmmText(preEnd) + " lower line (" + px(loH) + ")." + readyH)

// ── The resting stop: just past the current line, or the max-loss cap from the fill if that is closer.
// Re-placed every bar so it moves with the line. The cap is live from the fill bar, like a bracket order: placed
// with the entry, it is measured from the expected fill (the signal close plus a tick), then from the real fill.
if longPlaced or shortPlaced  // the placed entry's size and max loss, for its bracket and lock
    tQty := qPlaced
    tMaxLoss := mlPlaced
capPts = tMaxLoss > 0 and tQty > 0 ? tMaxLoss / tQty / syminfo.pointvalue : na
lineStopL = ub * (1 - stopBuf * sig)
lineStopS = lb * (1 + stopBuf * sig)
capL = na(capPts) ? na : strategy.position_size > 0 ? strategy.position_avg_price - capPts : longPlaced ? close + syminfo.mintick - capPts : na
capS = na(capPts) ? na : strategy.position_size < 0 ? strategy.position_avg_price + capPts : shortPlaced ? close - syminfo.mintick + capPts : na
longStop = na(capL) ? lineStopL : math.max(lineStopL, capL)
shortStop = na(capS) ? lineStopS : math.min(lineStopS, capS)
longWhy = not na(capL) and capL > lineStopL ? "Max loss" : "Back inside"
shortWhy = not na(capS) and capS < lineStopS ? "Max loss" : "Back inside"
// The lock: once a bar has reached lockAt max losses in profit, the stop moves to the entry plus lockPlus, from the next
// bar (a broker's auto-breakeven does it the moment price touches the trigger).
var bool locked = false
lockPts = useStop and lockAt > 0 and tMaxLoss > 0 and tQty > 0 ? lockAt * tMaxLoss / tQty / syminfo.pointvalue : na
if strategy.position_size == 0
    locked := false
else if not na(lockPts) and not locked
    locked := strategy.position_size > 0 ? high - strategy.position_avg_price >= lockPts : strategy.position_avg_price - low >= lockPts
lockL = locked and strategy.position_size > 0 ? strategy.position_avg_price + lockPlus : na
lockS = locked and strategy.position_size < 0 ? strategy.position_avg_price - lockPlus : na
if not na(lockL) and lockL > longStop
    longStop := lockL
    longWhy := "Lock"
if not na(lockS) and lockS < shortStop
    shortStop := lockS
    shortWhy := "Lock"
// The stop only ever tightens (v1.8, on by default; always in webhook mode, where the broker holds the stop placed with
// the entry and an exit message closes the trade when the chart's tighter stop fills).
var float heldL = na
var float heldS = na
var string heldWhyL = ""
var string heldWhyS = ""
if (useHook or tightenOnly) and useStop
    if strategy.position_size > 0 and not na(heldL) and heldL > longStop
        longStop := heldL
        longWhy := heldWhyL
    if strategy.position_size < 0 and not na(heldS) and heldS < shortStop
        shortStop := heldS
        shortWhy := heldWhyS
    heldL := strategy.position_size > 0 or longPlaced ? longStop : na
    heldS := strategy.position_size < 0 or shortPlaced ? shortStop : na
    heldWhyL := longWhy
    heldWhyS := shortWhy
// The take-profit limit: tpUnits noise units past the fill. It needs the fill price, so it starts the bar after the fill.
longTp = strategy.position_size > 0 and tpUnits > 0 ? strategy.position_avg_price * (1 + tpUnits * sig) : na
shortTp = strategy.position_size < 0 and tpUnits > 0 ? strategy.position_avg_price * (1 - tpUnits * sig) : na
if useStop and inRth and not na(ub)
    if strategy.position_size > 0 or longPlaced
        strategy.exit("Long exit", "Long", stop = longStop, limit = longTp, comment_loss = longWhy, comment_profit = "Target",
             alert_loss = useHook ? jsonExit : "EXIT LONG: price hit the stop at " + px(longStop) + ". Your stop should have filled. If you had no stop in, exit at market now.",
             alert_profit = useHook ? jsonExit : "TARGET: the long reached the take-profit at " + px(nz(longTp)) + ". Your limit should have filled. If not, exit at market now.")
    if strategy.position_size < 0 or shortPlaced
        strategy.exit("Short exit", "Short", stop = shortStop, limit = shortTp, comment_loss = shortWhy, comment_profit = "Target",
             alert_loss = useHook ? jsonExit : "EXIT SHORT: price hit the stop at " + px(shortStop) + ". Your stop should have filled. If you had no stop in, exit at market now.",
             alert_profit = useHook ? jsonExit : "TARGET: the short reached the take-profit at " + px(nz(shortTp)) + ". Your limit should have filled. If not, exit at market now.")

// The time stop (G6): a trade still losing timeStop minutes after its fill, and not locked, is closed at market.
var int tsFill = na
var float tsPrevPos = 0.0
if strategy.position_size != 0 and (tsPrevPos == 0 or (tsPrevPos > 0) != (strategy.position_size > 0))
    tsFill := bar_index
tsPrevPos := strategy.position_size
if timeStop > 0 and strategy.position_size != 0 and not locked and not na(tsFill) and not (inRth and endMin == RTH_CLOSE)
    if (bar_index + 1 - tsFill) * barMin >= timeStop and (strategy.position_size > 0 ? close < strategy.position_avg_price : close > strategy.position_avg_price)
        mark("EXIT", strategy.position_size < 0, color.gray)
        lastSignal := "EXIT (time stop) @ " + px(close)
        strategy.close_all(comment = "Time stop", alert_message = hookExit)
        say("EXIT: the trade is still losing " + str.tostring(timeStop) + " minutes after the fill. Close it at market now (time stop).")

nextText = not inRth or endMin >= LAST_CHECK ? "10:00 next session" : endMin < FIRST_CHECK ? "10:00" : hhmmText(endMin - (endMin - FIRST_CHECK) % 30 + 30)

// ── 16:00: flat, and store today's moves if the session was complete
if inRth and endMin == RTH_CLOSE
    if strategy.position_size != 0
        mark("FLAT", strategy.position_size < 0, color.gray)
        lastSignal := "FLAT 16:00 @ " + px(close)
        strategy.close_all(comment = "16:00 close", alert_message = hookExit, immediately = true)
        say("FLAT: close your MNQ position at market now (16:00 close).")
    if not na(dayOpen) and not na(dayHi)  // the session's record for the big-day rule
        array.push(dayRanges, (dayHi - dayLo) / dayOpen)
        array.push(dayDirs, close > dayOpen ? 1 : close < dayOpen ? -1 : 0)
        array.push(dayCloses, close)
        if array.size(dayCloses) > 300
            array.shift(dayCloses)
        if array.size(dayRanges) > 100
            array.shift(dayRanges)
            array.shift(dayDirs)
    if not na(dayOpen)
        complete = true
        for k = 0 to N_CHECKS - 1
            if na(array.get(today, k))
                complete := false
        if complete
            for k = 0 to N_CHECKS - 1
                array.set(moves, slot * N_CHECKS + k, array.get(today, k))
            slot := (slot + 1) % lookback
            filled += 1
    dayOpen := na

// ── Drawing
plot(showBands and inRth ? ub : na, "Upper noise line", color.teal, 2, plot.style_linebr)
plot(showBands and inRth ? lb : na, "Lower noise line", color.maroon, 2, plot.style_linebr)
bgcolor(shadeTrades and strategy.position_size > 0 ? color.new(color.teal, 88) : shadeTrades and strategy.position_size < 0 ? color.new(color.maroon, 88) : na)

var table dash = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 15, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 15), border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(color.gray, 60))
if showDash and (barstate.islastconfirmedhistory or barstate.isrealtime)
    pos = strategy.position_size
    status = not validTf ? "Use a 1/5/10/15/30 min chart" : filled < lookback ? "Building history" : pos > 0 ? "LONG" : pos < 0 ? "SHORT" : skipToday and inRth ? "No trades today (date list)" : "Flat"
    statusColor = pos > 0 ? color.lime : pos < 0 ? color.red : color.white
    closed = strategy.closedtrades
    todayPnlDash = strategy.netprofit - dayStartNet
    wins = strategy.wintrades
    table.cell(dash, 0, 0, "MNQ Noise Momentum v3.8: " + account + ", " + str.tostring(qty) + " MNQ", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 0, status, text_color = statusColor, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 0, 1, "Sessions of history", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 1, str.tostring(math.min(filled, lookback)) + " / " + str.tostring(lookback), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    // the next check's lines are known from the open: the same average of the last sessions' moves at that check
    nextEndD = not inRth or endMin >= LAST_CHECK ? na : endMin < FIRST_CHECK ? FIRST_CHECK : endMin - (endMin - FIRST_CHECK) % 30 + 30
    string nextLines = ""
    if not na(nextEndD) and not na(dayOpen) and not na(prevClose) and filled >= lookback
        kn = int((nextEndD - FIRST_CHECK) / 30)
        float sn = 0.0
        for d = 0 to lookback - 1
            sn += array.get(moves, d * N_CHECKS + kn)
        sgn = sn / lookback
        nextLines := "; at " + hhmmText(nextEndD) + ": " + px(math.max(dayOpen, prevClose) * (1 + sgn)) + " / " + px(math.min(dayOpen, prevClose) * (1 - sgn))
    table.cell(dash, 0, 2, "Upper / lower now, next", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 2, (na(ub) or not inRth ? "next lines at 10:00" : px(ub) + " / " + px(lb)) + nextLines, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 0, 3, "Next check", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 3, nextText + (headsUp != "" ? ": " + headsUp : ""), text_color = headsUp != "" ? color.yellow : color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 0, 4, "Backtest trades / win %", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 4, str.tostring(closed) + " / " + (closed > 0 ? str.tostring(100 * wins / closed, "#") + "%" : "-"), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 0, 6, "Last signal", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 6, lastSignal, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 0, 7, "Exit rule", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 7, (useStop ? "stop " + str.tostring(stopBuf) + " noise units past the line" + (na(lockPts) ? "" : ", lock at +" + px(lockPts)) : "half-hour check") + (useHook ? "; webhook orders on (" + hookSym + ")" : ""), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    tpNow = pos > 0 ? longTp : pos < 0 ? shortTp : na
    table.cell(dash, 0, 8, "Your stop / target", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 8, not useStop or pos == 0 ? "-" : px(pos > 0 ? longStop : shortStop) + " / " + (na(tpNow) ? "-" : px(tpNow)),
         text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 0, 9, "Today P/L", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 9, usd(todayPnlDash), text_color = todayPnlDash >= 0 ? color.lime : color.red, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 0, 10, "Open P/L", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 10, pos != 0 ? usd(strategy.openprofit) : "-", text_color = strategy.openprofit >= 0 ? color.lime : color.red, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 0, 11, "Trades today", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    losersNow = losersSince(dayStartClosed)
    doneToday = maxLosers > 0 and losersNow >= maxLosers
    roomText = budgetOn ? (budgetOk ? "; loss room " + usd(moneyRoom) + (qNext < qBase ? ", next trade " + str.tostring(qNext) + " MNQ" : ", up to " + str.tostring(qBase) + " MNQ") : "; loss limit reached") : ""
    table.cell(dash, 1, 11, str.tostring(closed - dayStartClosed) + (maxLosers > 0 ? " (" + str.tostring(losersNow) + " lost" + (doneToday ? ": done for today)" : ", limit " + str.tostring(maxLosers) + ")") : "") + roomText,
         text_color = doneToday or (budgetOn and not budgetOk) ? color.orange : color.white, text_size = size.small)
    capLate = maxLoss > 0 and useStop and barMin > 5
    table.cell(dash, 0, 12, "Chart", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    extHours = sawOvernight   // 24-hour bars: the 14 sessions of history use up most of the chart
    table.cell(dash, 1, 12, capLate ? "use 5 min: tested on 5-minute bars; on " + str.tostring(barMin) + " min the target starts " + str.tostring(barMin) + " min late" :
         str.tostring(barMin) + " min" + (extHours ? ", ETH: switch to RTH for about 4x more backtest days (same trades)" : ""),
         text_color = capLate or extHours ? color.orange : color.white, text_size = size.small)
    fedNow = fedToday and inRth and endMin < FED_CUTOFF
    table.cell(dash, 0, 13, "Fed day", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 13, fedNow ? "yes: no shorts until 14:00" : fedToday and inRth ? "yes: statement out, normal rules" : "no",
         text_color = fedNow ? color.orange : color.white, text_size = size.small)
    perContract = maxLoss / qty
    tight = maxLoss > 0 and perContract < 60
    table.cell(dash, 0, 14, "Max loss per contract", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 14, maxLoss <= 0 ? "off" : usd(perContract) + (tight ? ": tight, normal moves hit it (about $117 tested best)" : ""),
         text_color = tight ? color.orange : color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 0, 5, "Backtest net", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 5, (strategy.netprofit < 0 ? "-$" : "$") + str.tostring(math.abs(strategy.netprofit), "#,##0.00"),
         text_color = strategy.netprofit >= 0 ? color.lime : color.red, text_size = size.small)

// ── Trade log: every trade, exactly when it opened and closed, newest first
var table tlog = table.new(position.bottom_right, 7, 32, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 15), border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(color.gray, 60))
logCell(int col, int row, string txt, color c) =>
    table.cell(tlog, col, row, txt, text_color = c, text_size = size.small)
if showLog and (barstate.islastconfirmedhistory or barstate.isrealtime)
    table.clear(tlog, 0, 0, 6, 31)
    logCell(0, 0, "Opened (NY)", color.silver)
    logCell(1, 0, "Side", color.silver)
    logCell(2, 0, "Entry", color.silver)
    logCell(3, 0, "Closed (NY)", color.silver)
    logCell(4, 0, "Exit", color.silver)
    logCell(5, 0, "P/L", color.silver)
    logCell(6, 0, "Why", color.silver)
    int row = 1
    if strategy.opentrades > 0
        sz = strategy.opentrades.size(0)
        logCell(0, row, stamp(strategy.opentrades.entry_time(0)), color.white)
        logCell(1, row, (sz > 0 ? "LONG " : "SHORT ") + str.tostring(math.abs(sz)), sz > 0 ? color.lime : color.red)
        logCell(2, row, px(strategy.opentrades.entry_price(0)), color.white)
        logCell(3, row, "OPEN", color.yellow)
        logCell(4, row, px(close) + " now", color.white)
        logCell(5, row, usd(strategy.openprofit), strategy.openprofit >= 0 ? color.lime : color.red)
        openTp = sz > 0 ? longTp : shortTp
        logCell(6, row, not useStop ? "half-hour check" : "stop " + px(sz > 0 ? longStop : shortStop) + (na(openTp) ? "" : ", target " + px(openTp)), color.white)
        row += 1
    nLog = math.min(logRows, strategy.closedtrades)
    if nLog > 0
        for j = 0 to nLog - 1
            t = strategy.closedtrades - 1 - j
            sz = strategy.closedtrades.size(t)
            pl = strategy.closedtrades.profit(t)
            logCell(0, row, stamp(strategy.closedtrades.entry_time(t)), color.white)
            logCell(1, row, (sz > 0 ? "LONG " : "SHORT ") + str.tostring(math.abs(sz)), sz > 0 ? color.lime : color.red)
            logCell(2, row, px(strategy.closedtrades.entry_price(t)), color.white)
            logCell(3, row, stamp(strategy.closedtrades.exit_time(t)), color.white)
            logCell(4, row, px(strategy.closedtrades.exit_price(t)), color.white)
            logCell(5, row, usd(pl), pl >= 0 ? color.lime : color.red)
            logCell(6, row, why(strategy.closedtrades.exit_comment(t)), color.white)
            row += 1
// ── Evaluation tracker: the strategy's trades since the evaluation started, through the evaluation's rules, by
// end-of-day balance (the same walk as mnqbot.report.run_eval)
dayKey(int t) => year(t, TZ) * 10000 + month(t, TZ) * 100 + dayofmonth(t, TZ)
var table etab = table.new(position.bottom_left, 2, 7, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 15), border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(color.gray, 60))
if evalStart > 0 and (barstate.islastconfirmedhistory or barstate.isrealtime)
    float rel = 0.0
    float peak = 0.0
    float best = 0.0
    float dayPl = 0.0
    int curDay = 0
    int tdays = 0
    string state = "in progress"
    if strategy.closedtrades > 0
        for j = 0 to strategy.closedtrades - 1
            dk = dayKey(strategy.closedtrades.exit_time(j))
            if dk >= evalStart and state == "in progress"
                if curDay != 0 and dk != curDay   // the previous day is complete: its end-of-day balance counts
                    if rel + math.min(dayPl, 0) <= math.min(peak - evalDD, 0)
                        state := "FAILED"
                    rel += dayPl
                    tdays += 1
                    best := math.max(best, dayPl)
                    peak := math.max(peak, rel)
                    if state == "in progress" and rel >= evalTarget and tdays >= evalDays and (evalCons <= 0 or best < evalCons / 100 * rel)
                        state := "PASSED"
                    dayPl := 0.0
                curDay := dk
                dayPl += strategy.closedtrades.profit(j)
    if curDay != 0 and state == "in progress"   // the last day with trades, so far
        if rel + math.min(dayPl, 0) <= math.min(peak - evalDD, 0)
            state := "FAILED"
        rel += dayPl
        tdays += 1
        best := math.max(best, dayPl)
        peak := math.max(peak, rel)
        if state == "in progress" and rel >= evalTarget and tdays >= evalDays and (evalCons <= 0 or best < evalCons / 100 * rel)
            state := "PASSED"
    floorNow = math.min(peak - evalDD, 0)
    room = rel - floorNow
    fullLoss = maxLoss > 0 ? maxLoss + 2 * 0.62 * qty : na
    needed = evalCons > 0 ? math.max(evalTarget, best / (evalCons / 100)) : evalTarget
    stateColor = state == "PASSED" ? color.lime : state == "FAILED" ? color.red : color.white
    table.cell(etab, 0, 0, "Evaluation from " + str.tostring(evalStart), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(etab, 1, 0, state, text_color = stateColor, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(etab, 0, 1, "Profit", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(etab, 1, 1, usd(rel) + " of " + usd(evalTarget), text_color = rel >= 0 ? color.lime : color.red, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(etab, 0, 2, "Drawdown floor", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(etab, 1, 2, usd(floorNow) + ": " + usd(room) + " above it" + (na(fullLoss) ? "" : " (" + str.tostring(math.floor(room / fullLoss)) + " full losers)"),
         text_color = not na(fullLoss) and room < 2 * fullLoss ? color.orange : color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(etab, 0, 3, "Best day", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(etab, 1, 3, usd(best) + (rel > 0 ? " = " + str.tostring(100 * best / rel, "#") + "% of the profit" : "") + (evalCons > 0 ? " (needs under " + str.tostring(evalCons, "#") + "%)" : ""),
         text_color = evalCons > 0 and rel > 0 and best >= evalCons / 100 * rel ? color.orange : color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(etab, 0, 4, "To pass", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(etab, 1, 4, state == "PASSED" ? "done" : "profit of " + usd(needed) + " and " + str.tostring(evalDays) + " trading days", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(etab, 0, 5, "Trading days", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(etab, 1, 5, str.tostring(tdays), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(etab, 0, 6, "Note", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(etab, 1, 6, "from this chart's trades; your account's fills may differ", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.small)

prevClosed := strategy.closedtrades
